scene every-command

// ═══════════════════ EVERY COMMAND, ONCE ═══════════════════
// A witness example, not a genre guide. The twelve genre examples cover the
// commands a story reaches for daily; this one exercises what they never touch
// (save/load, wait, tint/blur, preload, text_pace, named animations, splines,
// queued lanes, stat-gated options) so that CAPABILITIES.md can not document a
// construct nothing compiles. The doc gate (tools/lvnconv/lvn/
// docs_contract_test.go) fails when a documented construct has no witness in
// howto/ or examples/ — this file is where the leftovers get their witness.
//
// It is still a real scene: a projectionist threads reel three and the machine
// argues back.

actor_map Ida=ida

// ─── Typing speed for the whole scene (chars/sec; 0 = instant) ───
text_pace cps=45

// ─── Warm the assets the scene is about to need (non-blocking) ───
preload url="/content/bg/projection.jpg" kind=sprite
preload url="/content/sfx/projector.ogg" kind=audio

bg /content/bg/projection.jpg
actor ida left neutral scale=1 rotation=0
Ida: Reel three. Let's see if the lamp holds this time.

// ─── Snapshot: the "watch it again" option below rewinds to exactly here ───
save slot="booth"

// ─── A warm veil plus a blur = the beam coming up ───
tint color="#f0c070" alpha=0.25 duration=0.6
blur alpha=0.35 duration=0.5
wait ms=400
The beam catches the dust in the air.
blur alpha=0 duration=0.4

// ─── Animation: one property per lane, so these three play at once ───
anim id=ida prop=rotation keys="0:-3 1:3 2:-3" loop=yoyo ease=inOutSine
anim ida scale to=1.04 dur=0.6 ease=outBack
anim ida alpha to=0.85 dur=0.4 ease=linear   // the house lights drop on her

// ─── A named animation: defined once (emits nothing), stamped on anybody ───
defanim rattle prop=x keys="0:0 0.05:-0.02 0.1:0.02 0.15:0" loop=restart
play id=ida anim=rattle
Ida: Hear that? The film gate is rattling again.
anim ida stop

// ─── One lane, in order: mode=queue waits for the step before it ───
anim id=ida channel=pace prop=screen_x to=0.34 dur=0.8 ease=outCubic
anim id=ida channel=pace prop=screen_x to=0.20 dur=0.8 ease=inBack mode=queue

// ─── A path: spline through the waypoints, nose along the tangent ───
move id=ida path="0.20,0.62 0.50,0.55 0.78,0.62" dur=1.6 interp=spline orient=true ease=outCubic
wait ms=200

// ─── Squash and stretch: two axes, one of them stepped (values snap) ───
anim id=ida prop=scalex keys="0:1 0.2:1.06 0.4:1" ease=inOutSine loop=once
anim id=ida prop=scaley keys="0:1 0.2:0.94 0.4:1" interp=step loop=once
Ida: There. Threaded.

// ─── A stat gate on an option: too low, and the option is HIDDEN ───
// (`requires_stat` + `min` hide it — they do not grey it out.)
lamp = 2
Ida: The lamp is at {lamp} of 3. What do we do?

- Push the lamp to full -> forced requires_stat=lamp min=3
- Thread it by hand and run it soft -> soft
- Rewind and watch the reel again -> again

:forced
// Unreachable while lamp < 3 — that is the point of the gate.
Ida: Full power. Bold.
-> reel

:soft
Ida: Soft it is. The audience will never know.
-> reel

:again
// `load` restores the snapshot and redraws the scene from that point.
load slot="booth"
-> reel

:reel
tint color="#f0c070" alpha=0 duration=0.5
wait ms=300
The reel runs out. The house lights come up.
-> __end
